1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
She has grown a beautiful harvest.
Now she wants to sell it online.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
The gift boxes are ready.
But reaching buyers is unfamiliar territory.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Where should she start?
She needs help taking product photos.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Nearby, a young resident has
a slow afternoon with nothing planned.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
He has time and a camera.
He just has not found a local opportunity.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
A paid photography task nearby
gives him a reason to get involved.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Village Jobs helps them connect
and arrange the work directly.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,400
A useful first step toward selling her harvest.
Here is how the connection works.

9
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:37,400
Let us follow one paid photography task.
From posting to the first conversation.

10
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:42,400
English is the default.
Korean is also available.

11
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:47,900
Text is the default.
Every field is visible.

12
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:53,400
Voice is optional.
Posting starts without sign-in.

13
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:59,900
Meta Muse Spark extracts
the conditions stated in the text.

14
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:06,400
Place, timing, pay and people needed.
These fields came from the live model response.

15
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:12,900
The model does not make the final decision.

16
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:19,400
The farmer edits the pay and description,
then checks the date and time.

17
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:23,400
After review, the opportunity is published.

18
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:27,400
The creator can edit or close it
from the same browser.

19
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:32,400
A young person searches by town
and opens the details.

20
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:37,400
Place, time and pay are visible
without sign-in.

21
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:41,900
Applying requires verification.

22
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:46,400
This recording uses a local test code.
No email was sent.

23
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:52,900
The applicant adds a name and note,
then chooses a phone number or email.

24
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:59,400
Sharing that contact with this farmer
requires explicit consent.

25
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:05,900
The farmer sees the shared contact
inside My jobs.

26
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:12,400
They arrange the work and payment directly.
The app does not process payments.

27
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:18,400
Withdrawing hides the contact
from subsequent farmer requests.

28
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:24,400
It cannot take back information
the farmer has already seen.

29
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:31,900
Data currently lives in server memory
and resets when the server restarts.

30
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:39,400
Real-user validation and effects on
rural population retention remain unproven.

31
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:44,400
Discover an opportunity to work
closer to home.

32
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:49,400
Village Jobs helps start
the first conversation.

